  "details": "UI elements are generally speaking not affected by the lighting of the world, but for some reason they have an angle based highlight (may be a matcap, or some other affect) that in some conditions makes it harder to read text. (Not quite so extreme example here, but still an example)\n\nI think an affect to make the UI feel less flat is good in theory, but having it based on viewing angle is visually distracting, and feels very out of place in non-VR platforms.\n\nI'd always considered making a feedback post about it, but in the recent HUD update it's even begun affecting the mic icon. Making it look like my mic is activating or flickering sometimes when nothing is happening other than me turning. Picture of that too, the mic icon in 2 different angles. It doesn't look too drastic in isolation, but in game it just feels off.",
